menu "QUTEE settings"

    config MICRO_ROS_APP_STACK
        int "Stack the micro-ROS app (Bytes)"
        default 16000
        help
        Stack size in Bytes of the micro-ROS app

    config MICRO_ROS_APP_TASK_PRIO
        int "Priority of the micro-ROS app"
        default 1
        help
        Priority of micro-ros task higher value means higher priority

    config ROBOT_CTRL_APP_STACK
        int "Stack the Robot Controll app (Bytes)"
        default 16000
        help
        Stack size in Bytes of the Robot Controll app

    config ROBOT_CTRL_APP_TASK_PRIO
        int "Priority of the Robot Controll app"
        default 10
        help
        Priority of  Robot Controll task higher value means higher priority

    config NB_HIDDEN_LAYERS 
        int "Number of Hidden Layers in the neural network"
        default 1
        help
        Number of Hidden Layers in the neural network


    config NB_NEURONS_PER_LAYER
        int "Number of neuron per hidden layer"
        default 10
        help
        Number of neuron per hidden layer. Every hidden layer has the same size. 
    config QUTEE_NAME
        string "Name of the Qutee robot"
        default "qutee"
        help
        Name of the Qutee robot. Useful if multiple robots are used. This is used as prefix for the ROS2 topic/service names. 
        
    config CONTROL_FREQUENCY
        int "Control freqency for the Qutee, in Hz"
        default 50
        help
        Control freqency for the Qutee

    config EPISODE_DURATION
        int "Duration of an episode in seconds"
        default 5
        help
        Duration of an episode

    config LEG_UP_ANGLE
        int "Leg angle that puts the torso on the ground (degrees)"
        default 60
        range 0 90
        help
        At boot, the legs are first raised by this angle (joint 2 of each leg) so that the torso
        rests on the ground, then lowered to the rest pose. 0 is the standing pose.

    config LEG_REST_ANGLE
        int "Leg angle of the rest pose (degrees)"
        default 35
        range 0 90
        help
        Rest pose, used after boot and between rollouts: the legs are raised by this angle (joint 2
        of each leg). 0 is the standing pose. With "Turn the motors' torque off in the rest pose",
        use an angle at which the torso already rests on the ground: if the legs still carry the
        robot when they go limp, the torso drops and the joints are back-driven fast, which can
        trip the motors.

    config QUTEE_LOG_UDP_PORT
        int "UDP port for the logs over WiFi (0 = off)"
        default 8889
        range 0 65535
        help
        In ROS mode, once WiFi is connected, the robot also sends its logs (starting with the
        ones since boot) to the micro-ROS agent's IP on this UDP port. Read them with
        software/tools/wifi_monitor.py. Lines containing "password" are never sent.

    config TORQUE_OFF_AT_REST
        bool "Turn the motors' torque off in the rest pose"
        default y
        help
        Saves battery and keeps the motors cool between rollouts: once the robot reaches the rest
        pose, the motors go limp and the torso settles on the ground. The torque comes back on
        before the next move. Turn this off to keep the legs held in place (for example when the
        robot hangs on a stand).

    config POSE_TRANSITION_TIME_MS
        int "Duration of a slow move between poses (ms)"
        default 1000
        range 100 10000
        help
        Time taken to move between the rest pose, the standing pose and the pose at the end of
        a rollout.

    
endmenu